# `=` in the condition of `iff`: DS0110, not a named argument.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | extend big = iff(amount = 100, "yes", "no")
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..64
  PIPELINE@0..63
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    EXTEND_OP@20..63
      IDENT@20..26 "extend"
      WHITESPACE@26..27 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@27..63
        NAME@27..30
          IDENT@27..30 "big"
        WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
        EQ@31..32 "="
        WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
        CALL_EXPR@33..63
          NAME_REF@33..36
            IDENT@33..36 "iff"
          ARG_LIST@36..63
            L_PAREN@36..37 "("
            BIN_EXPR@37..49
              NAME_REF@37..43
                IDENT@37..43 "amount"
              WHITESPACE@43..44 " "
              EQ@44..45 "="
              WHITESPACE@45..46 " "
              LITERAL@46..49
                LONG@46..49 "100"
            COMMA@49..50 ","
            WHITESPACE@50..51 " "
            LITERAL@51..56
              STRING@51..56 "\"yes\""
            COMMA@56..57 ","
            WHITESPACE@57..58 " "
            LITERAL@58..62
              STRING@58..62 "\"no\""
            R_PAREN@62..63 ")"
  WHITESPACE@63..64 "\n"

error[DS0110]: `=` is assignment, not comparison
  --> query:1:45
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | extend big = iff(amount = 100, "yes", "no")
  |                                             ^ assignment is not allowed here
  |
  = help: use `==` to compare values: `amount == 100`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | extend big = iff(amount == 100, "yes", "no")
which parses without errors
